module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.CechCompletionSlice
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.LocalizationCompletion
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Derived completion commutes with restriction to a localized ringed site

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪` and let `U` be an
object of `𝒞`. `CechCompletionSlice.lean` identified the completion functor of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] on the slice with the restriction of the one upstairs, by an isomorphism
`K^∧|_U ≅ (K|_U)^∧` natural in `K`. This file proves that that isomorphism carries the completion
map `K|_U ⟶ (K|_U)^∧` to the restriction of `K ⟶ K^∧`, and deduces, for the sheaf of ideals
`ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)`, the assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F]: **the canonical map
`a : (K|_U)^∧ ⟶ K^∧|_U` is an isomorphism, for every `K`.** `OverIdealComparison.lean` restates
that with the completion on the slice taken along the restriction `ℐ|_U` and packages it as a
natural isomorphism of functors. The Remark for a sheaf of ideals of finite type is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion_restrict` of
`LocalizationCompletionFiniteType.lean`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso`: `𝒪[0]|_U ≅ 𝒪_U[0]` as
  complexes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso`: the same in `D(𝒪_U)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.complexMap_comp_structureSheafHomEvaluation`: at the chain level,
  the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 08JB] out of the structure sheaf complex, followed by evaluation
  at the unit section on the slice, is the restriction of evaluation at the unit section.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict`: **the restriction of
  `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K) ≅ K` is `R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪_U}(𝒪_U, K|_U) ≅ K|_U`**, under [Stacks, Tag 08JB].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overFunctor_map_cechAugmentation_comp` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overFunctor_mapDerivedCategory_map_cechAugmentation_comp`: the
  identification `Č(f)|_U ≅ Č(f|_U)` carries the restriction of the augmentation
  `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]` to the augmentation of the slice, as a map of complexes and then in `D(𝒪_U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overFunctor_map_completionUnit_comp` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit_comp_completionFunctorRestrictIso_inv`: **the
  completion map of [Stacks, Tag 099B] restricts to the completion map of the slice.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionRestrictComparisonGlobalSections_app`:
  the invertibility of the map `a` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] at every `K`, for `ℐ` generated by
  finitely many global sections and `ℐ|_U` generated on the slice by their restrictions. Restated
  at the restriction `ℐ|_U` itself, and packaged as a natural isomorphism, in
  `OverIdealComparison.lean`.

## Implementation notes

*The two halves.* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit` is the identification
`K = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K)` followed by the map which the augmentation `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]` induces on
derived internal Hom into `K`, so the compatibility splits accordingly. The augmentation half is
the chain-level
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overFunctor_map_extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp` of
`CechSliceRestriction.lean`, which compares the augmentations `𝒪 ⟶ Č(f)^0` in the other
direction; the two augmentations of the degree-zero term are mutually inverse, because the index
type in degree zero is a singleton, which turns one statement into the other, and both sides are
maps into a complex concentrated in degree zero, so the passage from the degree-zero term to the
complex is `HomologicalComplex.to_single_hom_ext`.

The structure-sheaf half is the harder one: both identifications
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedStructureSheafHomIso` and
`(AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedHomRestriction X U).iso` are pinned down only on
K-injective representatives, so the comparison is made at the chain level, through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restrictionSourceComparison` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restrictionTargetComparison`. At a K-injective `I` the two model
characterizations turn the statement into `complexMap_comp_structureSheafHomEvaluation`, every
restriction comparison in sight cancelling against its inverse; and both sides are natural in
`K`, so the K-injective model of an arbitrary `K` transports it.

*Why several statements go through abstract lemmas.* Sheaves of modules on the slice are indexed
by `(X.over U).ringSheaf` when they come from the slice ringed site and by `X.ringSheaf.over U`
when they come from restriction along `CategoryTheory.Over.forget U`, and the degree-`p` term of
a restricted complex is `(K|_U)^p` in one spelling and `(K^p)|_U` in the other. Each of those
pairs is the same object, but only after a definition that is not reducible is unfolded, so a
composite that crosses from one spelling to the other is ill-typed at the transparency a rewrite
uses and every rewrite on it fails. Making the functors involved locally `implicit_reducible`, as
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/InternalHom/DerivedHomRestriction.lean` does, is
enough for most of the goals here but not for the ones that compose with the unit sheaf or with a
product projection; those are reduced by a single `exact` to one of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inv_comp_eq_comp_inv_of`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.comp_eq_comp_inv_of_comp_comp`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.comp_comp_eq_comp_comp`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.map_op_app_comp_map_op_app_assoc` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.map_comp_map_assoc`, which are stated in one abstract category
where the rewriting is unproblematic.

*Which ideal sheaf.* The final statement is about the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many
global sections upstairs and the one generated *on the slice* by their restrictions, not about
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal`: those are the two ideal sheaves for which
[Stacks, Tag 099B] gives a reflector with no hypothesis, and they are not known to agree — that
is the sheafification question of [Stacks, Tag 099E]. The map `a` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionRestrictComparisonGlobalSections`, which is built
for exactly this pair.

*Which statements carry a `stacks` attribute.* None. The compatibilities proved on
the way are not assertions of any source result: neither [Stacks, Tag 08JB] nor
[Stacks, Tag 08JD] states that the identification of the derived internal Hom out of the
structure sheaf with the identity commutes with restriction to a slice, and [Stacks, Tag 099B]
does not separately state the restriction of its completion map. The invertibility of `a` here
is [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] for a sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many global sections; the tag is
registered on its statement for a sheaf of ideals of finite type,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion_restrict` of
`LocalizationCompletionFiniteType.lean`.

*The Remark's second map.* `b : K^∧ ⟶ Rj_*((K|_U)^∧)` belongs to the Remark's alternative
argument; it is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion_restrict_secondMap` of
`LocalizationCompletionPushforward.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0996](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0996)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0F)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v₁ v₂

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

-- The finite (co)products of `D(O)` are those of its triangulated structure, as in the lemmas
-- used below, and not those of the instances of Stacks 07D9.
attribute [-instance] Stacks.Injectives.hasCoproducts_derivedCategory
  Stacks.Injectives.hasProducts_derivedCategory

attribute [local implicit_reducible]
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
  CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuous
  CochainComplex.HomComplex
  ModuleCat.restrictScalars
  ModuleCat.RestrictScalars.obj'
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀Obj
  PresheafOfModules.presheaf
  PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf
  PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars
  PresheafOfModules.restrictScalarsObj
  SheafOfModules.pushforward
  SheafOfModules.overFunctor
  SheafOfModules.toSheaf
  SheafOfModules.forget

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] (U : X.C)
  [HasWeakSheafify (X.over U).J CommRingCat.{u}]

/-- The restriction of the structure sheaf complex to the slice over `U` is the structure sheaf
complex of the slice: restriction is additive and carries the structure sheaf to the structure
sheaf, so it commutes with placing a module in degree zero. -/
def restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso :
    restrictComplex X (structureSheafComplex X) U ≅ structureSheafComplex (X.over U) :=
  (HomologicalComplex.singleMapHomologicalComplex
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).app _

/-- The identification of the restricted structure sheaf complex with the structure sheaf
complex of the slice carries the unit section to the unit section. -/
theorem restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso_inv_f_zero_one (V : Over U) :
    ((restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv.f 0).val.app (op V)
        (structureSheafOne (X.over U) V) =
      structureSheafOne X V.left := rfl

/-- In degree zero the identification of the restricted structure sheaf complex with the
structure sheaf complex of the slice is, after the identification of the degree-zero term of a
complex concentrated there with the object, the identity. -/
theorem overFunctor_map_singleObjXSelf_inv_comp_restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).map
          (HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf (ComplexShape.up ℤ) (0 : ℤ)
            (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).inv ≫
        (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).hom.f 0 =
      (HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf (ComplexShape.up ℤ) (0 : ℤ)
        (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over U).O)))).inv := rfl

/-- The chain-level comparison of [Stacks, Tag 08JB] acts on sections by evaluating the original
Hom section: `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.DerivedHomRestriction.complexMap_apply` read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.applyHomSection`. -/
theorem applyHomSection_complexMap (r : DerivedHomRestriction X U)
    (A B : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) (V : Over U) (n p q : ℤ)
    (hpq : p + n = q)
    (s : ((sheafHomComplex X A B).obj.X n).val.obj (op V.left))
    (x : ((restrictComplex X A U).X p).val.obj (op V)) :
    applyHomSection (X.over U)
        (sheafHomComplex (X.over U) (restrictComplex X A U) (restrictComplex X B U))
        V n p q hpq (((r.complexMap A B).f n).val.app (op V) s) x =
      applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X A B) V.left n p q hpq s x :=
  DerivedHomRestriction.complexMap_apply X U r A B (op V) (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V))) n p q hpq s x

/-- **Restriction carries evaluation at the unit section to evaluation at the unit section.**
On sections, the chain-level comparison of [Stacks, Tag 08JB] out of the structure sheaf complex,
followed by the identification of the restricted structure sheaf complex with the structure sheaf
complex of the slice and then by evaluation at the unit section there, evaluates the original Hom
section at the unit section upstairs. -/
private theorem applyHomSection_homMap_complexMap_one
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) (V : Over U) (n : ℤ)
    (s : ((sheafHomComplex X (structureSheafComplex X) I).obj.X n).val.obj (op V.left)) :
    applyHomSection (X.over U)
        (sheafHomComplex (X.over U) (structureSheafComplex (X.over U))
          (restrictComplex X I U)) V n 0 n (zero_add n)
        (((homMap (X.over U) (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv
              (𝟙 (restrictComplex X I U))).f n).val.app (op V)
          ((((derivedHomRestriction X U).complexMap (structureSheafComplex X) I).f n).val.app
            (op V) s))
        (structureSheafOne (X.over U) V) =
      applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X (structureSheafComplex X) I) V.left n 0 n (zero_add n)
        s (structureSheafOne X V.left) :=
  (applyHomSection_homMap (X.over U) (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv
      (𝟙 (restrictComplex X I U)) V n 0 n (zero_add n) _
      (structureSheafOne (X.over U) V)).trans
    (applyHomSection_complexMap X U (derivedHomRestriction X U) (structureSheafComplex X) I V
      n 0 n (zero_add n) s _)

/-- **The chain-level identification of [Stacks, Tag 08JB] at first argument `𝒪` is compatible
with evaluation at the unit section.** Restricting `SheafHom(𝒪, I) ≅ I` to the slice over `U` and
reading the source through the structure sheaf complex of the slice gives the identification
`SheafHom(𝒪_U, I|_U) ≅ I|_U` of the slice. -/
theorem complexMap_comp_structureSheafHomEvaluation
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) :
    (derivedHomRestriction X U).complexMap (structureSheafComplex X) I ≫
        homMap (X.over U) (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv
          (𝟙 (restrictComplex X I U)) ≫
        structureSheafHomEvaluation (X.over U) (restrictComplex X I U) =
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map (structureSheafHomEvaluation X I) :=
  HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n ↦ SheafOfModules.hom_ext
    (PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun V ↦ ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun s ↦
      applyHomSection_homMap_complexMap_one X U I V.unop n s))

section Abstract

/-- Two maps of a category whose composite one way round is the identity induce, after an
opposite-variance functor into a functor category and evaluation, a composite that cancels.

Stated abstractly, and consumed by `exact`/`rw`, because the two spellings of the category of
sheaves of modules on a slice are not identified at the transparency a rewrite uses; see the
implementation notes. -/
theorem map_op_app_comp_map_op_app_assoc {D E : Type*} [Category.{v₁} D] [Category.{v₂} E]
    (G : Dᵒᵖ ⥤ D ⥤ E) {A B : D} (α : A ⟶ B) (β : B ⟶ A) (h : β ≫ α = 𝟙 B) (Z : D)
    {W : E} (φ : (G.obj (op B)).obj Z ⟶ W) :
    (G.map α.op).app Z ≫ (G.map β.op).app Z ≫ φ = φ := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← NatTrans.comp_app, ← G.map_comp, ← op_comp, h, op_id,
    CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, NatTrans.id_app, Category.id_comp]

/-- Reassociation against a known composite, stated in one abstract category so that it can be
applied by `exact` across the two spellings of the category of sheaves of modules on a slice. -/
theorem comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq {D : Type*} [Category.{v₁} D] {A B C E : D} {a : A ⟶ B} {b : B ⟶ C}
    {d : A ⟶ C} (h : a ≫ b = d) (c : C ⟶ E) : a ≫ b ≫ c = d ≫ c := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, h]

/-- Transposing an identity of isomorphisms, in one abstract category. -/
theorem inv_comp_eq_comp_inv_of {D : Type*} [Category.{v₁} D] {A B C C' : D} (e : A ≅ B) (g : C ≅ C')
    {a : A ⟶ C} {b : B ⟶ C'} (h : a ≫ g.hom = e.hom ≫ b) : e.inv ≫ a = b ≫ g.inv := by
  rw [Iso.inv_comp_eq, ← Category.assoc, ← h, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- Moving an isomorphism out of the right-hand end of a composite, in one abstract category. -/
theorem comp_eq_comp_inv_of_comp_comp {D : Type*} [Category.{v₁} D] {A B C E : D} {a : A ⟶ B}
    {b : B ⟶ C} {d : A ⟶ E} (e : C ≅ E) (h : a ≫ b ≫ e.hom = d) : a ≫ b = d ≫ e.inv := by
  rw [← h, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- Rewriting the first two factors of a triple composite, in one abstract category. -/
theorem comp_comp_eq_comp_comp {D : Type*} [Category.{v₁} D] {A B B' C E : D} {a : A ⟶ B} {b : B ⟶ C}
    {a' : A ⟶ B'} {b' : B' ⟶ C} (h : a ≫ b = a' ≫ b') (c : C ⟶ E) :
    a ≫ b ≫ c = a' ≫ b' ≫ c := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, h, Category.assoc]

/-- The same cancellation for a covariant functor. -/
theorem map_comp_map_assoc {D E : Type*} [Category.{v₁} D] [Category.{v₂} E] (G : D ⥤ E) {A B : D}
    (α : A ⟶ B) (β : B ⟶ A) (h : α ≫ β = 𝟙 A) {W : E} (φ : G.obj A ⟶ W) :
    G.map α ≫ G.map β ≫ φ = φ := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← G.map_comp, h, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, Category.id_comp]

end Abstract

/-- `𝒪[0]|_U ≅ 𝒪_U[0]` in the derived category of the localized ringed site. -/
def derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj
        (derivedStructureSheaf X) ≅ derivedStructureSheaf (X.over U) :=
  restrictionComparison X U (structureSheafComplex X) ≪≫
    DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U)

/-- The identification of the restriction of the class of a complex with the class of its
degreewise restriction is natural. -/
theorem restrictionComparison_naturality
    {A B : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ} (g : A ⟶ B) :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map g) ≫ (restrictionComparison X U B).hom =
      (restrictionComparison X U A).hom ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map
        (((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map g) :=
  (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.hom.naturality g

private theorem derivedHomRestriction_iso_structureSheaf_hom_eq
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) [I.IsKInjective] :
    ((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso (derivedStructureSheaf X)
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)).hom =
      (restrictionSourceComparison X U (structureSheafComplex X) I).hom ≫
        DerivedCategory.Q.map
            ((derivedHomRestriction X U).complexMap (structureSheafComplex X) I) ≫
          (restrictionTargetComparison X U (structureSheafComplex X) I).inv :=
  ((Iso.eq_comp_inv (restrictionTargetComparison X U (structureSheafComplex X) I)).2
    (derivedHomRestriction_model X U (structureSheafComplex X) I)).trans
      (Category.assoc _ _ _)

/-- Restriction to the slice preserves K-injectivity, at the spelling `(X.over U).ringSheaf` of
the sheaf of rings in which sheaves of modules on the slice ringed site are indexed. This is
[Stacks, Tag 08FI], `Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.isKInjective_over`, which states it at the
spelling `X.ringSheaf.over U`; the two are the same object, but not reducibly, so instance
synthesis does not get from one to the other on its own. -/
private theorem isKInjective_restrictComplex_over
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) [I.IsKInjective] :
    CochainComplex.IsKInjective
      (show CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over U).O)) ℤ from
        restrictComplex X I U) :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.isKInjective_over X.J (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U I

attribute [local instance] isKInjective_restrictComplex_over

/-- Replacing the first argument of the internal Hom complex of the slice by the structure sheaf
complex of the slice, read on the K-injective model comparison of derived internal Hom. -/
private theorem derivedSheafHomComparison_restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso_inv
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) [I.IsKInjective] :
    ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv).op).app
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (restrictComplex X I U)) ≫
      (derivedSheafHomComparison (X.over U) (structureSheafComplex (X.over U))
        (restrictComplex X I U)).hom =
    (derivedSheafHomComparison (X.over U) (restrictComplex X (structureSheafComplex X) U)
        (restrictComplex X I U)).hom ≫
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (homMap (X.over U) (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv
        (𝟙 (restrictComplex X I U))) := by
  simpa using derivedSheafHomComparison_naturality (X.over U)
    (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv (𝟙 (restrictComplex X I U))

/-- The same statement with the K-injective model comparison of the slice replaced, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedStructureSheafHomIso_model`, by the identification of the
derived internal Hom out of the structure sheaf of the slice with the identity. -/
private theorem derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso_inv
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) [I.IsKInjective] :
    ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv).op).app
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (restrictComplex X I U)) ≫
      (@Iso.hom _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (restrictComplex X I U)))) =
    (derivedSheafHomComparison (X.over U) (restrictComplex X (structureSheafComplex X) U)
        (restrictComplex X I U)).hom ≫
      DerivedCategory.Q.map
        (homMap (X.over U) (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv
            (𝟙 (restrictComplex X I U)) ≫
          structureSheafHomEvaluation (X.over U) (restrictComplex X I U)) := by
  rw [derivedStructureSheafHomIso_model, ← Category.assoc,
    derivedSheafHomComparison_restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso_inv, Category.assoc,
    DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp]

/-- The slice half of the comparison: everything in the model identification of [Stacks,
Tag 08JB] below the source comparison collapses, by the cancellations of the restriction
comparisons, to the chain-level statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.complexMap_comp_structureSheafHomEvaluation`. -/
private theorem derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict_tail
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) [I.IsKInjective] :
    DerivedCategory.Q.map
          ((derivedHomRestriction X U).complexMap (structureSheafComplex X) I) ≫
        (restrictionTargetComparison X U (structureSheafComplex X) I).inv ≫
          ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
              (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).symm.op.hom).app
            ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj
              (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)) ≫
            (@Iso.hom _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)))) ≫
              (restrictionComparison X U I).hom =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map
        (((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map (structureSheafHomEvaluation X I)) := by
  rw [← derivedStructureSheafHomIso_naturality (X.over U) (restrictionComparison X U I).hom]
  simp only [restrictionTargetComparison, derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso, Iso.trans_inv,
    Iso.symm_hom, Iso.symm_inv, Iso.op_hom, Iso.op_inv, Functor.mapIso_inv, Iso.app_hom,
    Iso.app_inv, op_comp, Functor.map_comp, NatTrans.comp_app, Category.assoc]
  rw [map_op_app_comp_map_op_app_assoc (derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)) _ _
      (Iso.inv_hom_id_app
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategoryFactors
        (structureSheafComplex X)),
    ← NatTrans.naturality_assoc,
    map_comp_map_assoc _ _ _
      (Iso.inv_hom_id_app
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategoryFactors I),
    derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso_inv X U I,
    Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp,
    complexMap_comp_structureSheafHomEvaluation X U I]

private theorem derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict_aux
    (I : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) [I.IsKInjective] :
    ((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso (derivedStructureSheaf X)
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)).hom ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).symm.op.hom).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj
            (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)) ≫
        (@Iso.hom _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)))) =
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
        (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X (DerivedCategory.Q.obj I)).hom := by
  refine (cancel_mono (restrictionComparison X U I).hom).mp ?_
  rw [derivedHomRestriction_iso_structureSheaf_hom_eq X U I,
    derivedStructureSheafHomIso_model X I, Functor.map_comp]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [restrictionComparison_naturality X U (structureSheafHomEvaluation X I),
    restrictionSourceComparison]
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Functor.mapIso_hom, Category.assoc, cancel_epi]
  exact derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict_tail X U I

/-- Both sides of the comparison are natural in `K`: on the left by the naturality of
[Stacks, Tag 08JB] in its covariant variable, of the derived internal Hom bifunctor of the slice
in its first variable, and of the identification of the derived internal Hom out of the structure
sheaf of the slice with the identity; on the right by the last of those upstairs. -/
private theorem derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict_natural
    {K K' : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))} (φ : K ⟶ K') :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (derivedStructureSheaf X))).map φ) ≫
        (((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso (derivedStructureSheaf X) K').hom ≫
          ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
              (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).symm.op.hom).app
            ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K') ≫
            (@Iso.hom _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K')))) =
      (((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso (derivedStructureSheaf X) K).hom ≫
          ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
              (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).symm.op.hom).app
            ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) ≫
            (@Iso.hom _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K)))) ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map φ := by
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [reassoc_of% ((derivedHomRestriction X U).natural_right φ), NatTrans.naturality_assoc,
    derivedStructureSheafHomIso_naturality (X.over U)
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map φ)]

/-- **The restriction of the identification `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K) ≅ K` is the identification
`R𝑆heafHom_{𝒪_U}(𝒪_U, K|_U) ≅ K|_U` of the slice**, under [Stacks, Tag 08JB] and the
identification `𝒪[0]|_U ≅ 𝒪_U[0]`.

Both identifications are pinned only on K-injective representatives, so the statement is proved
at the class of a K-injective complex, where both become the chain-level
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.complexMap_comp_structureSheafHomEvaluation`, and then transported
to an arbitrary `K` along its K-injective model by the naturality of both sides. -/
theorem derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    ((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso (derivedStructureSheaf X) K).hom ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).symm.op.hom).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) ≫
          (@Iso.hom _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K))) =
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
        (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).hom := by
  have h2 : (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (derivedStructureSheaf X))).map
            (kInjectiveModelIso X K).inv) ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X
            (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (kInjectiveModel X K))).hom =
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).hom ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (kInjectiveModelIso X K).inv := by
    rw [← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp,
      derivedStructureSheafHomIso_naturality X (kInjectiveModelIso X K).inv]
  refine (cancel_mono ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
    (kInjectiveModelIso X K).inv)).mp ?_
  rw [← derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict_natural X U (kInjectiveModelIso X K).inv, ← h2,
    derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict_aux X U (kInjectiveModel X K)]

section Augmentation

variable {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- **The two augmentations of the degree-zero term of the Čech complex are mutually inverse.**
The degree-zero term is the single factor `𝒪_{f_∅}`, the canonical map `𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪_{f_∅}` is the
augmentation out of `𝒪`, and the identification `𝒪_{f_∅} ⟶ 𝒪` of `Completion.lean` is the
projection followed by its inverse. -/
theorem extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_cechAugmentationZero :
    extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation X f ≫ cechAugmentationZero X f =
      𝟙 (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
  (comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq (extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_pi X f default)
    (unitIsoAwayModuleEmpty X f).inv).trans (unitIsoAwayModuleEmpty X f).hom_inv_id

/-- The composite in the other order, which
`extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_cechAugmentationZero` gives because the degree-zero
identification is invertible. -/
theorem cechAugmentationZero_comp_extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation :
    cechAugmentationZero X f ≫ extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation X f =
      𝟙 ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).X 0) := by
  have := isIso_cechAugmentationZero X f
  rw [← cancel_mono (cechAugmentationZero X f), Category.assoc,
    extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_cechAugmentationZero, Category.comp_id,
    Category.id_comp]

/-- The degree-zero term of the Čech complex is `𝒪` compatibly with restriction to the slice:
the identification `Č(f)^0 ⟶ 𝒪` restricts to the identification `Č(f|_U)^0 ⟶ 𝒪_U`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overFunctor_map_extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp`,
which states the same for the augmentations in the other direction, together with the fact that
the two augmentations are mutually inverse. -/
theorem overFunctor_map_cechAugmentationZero_comp :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).map (cechAugmentationZero X f) =
      (extendedAlternatingCechOverIso X U f).hom.f 0 ≫
        cechAugmentationZero (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)) := by
  have : IsIso (extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation X f) :=
    ⟨⟨cechAugmentationZero X f,
      extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_cechAugmentationZero X f,
      cechAugmentationZero_comp_extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation X f⟩⟩
  refine (cancel_epi ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).map
    (extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation X f))).mp ?_
  rw [← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp,
    extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_cechAugmentationZero X f,
    CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
  exact ((comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq
    (overFunctor_map_extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp X U f)
    (cechAugmentationZero (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)))).trans
      (extendedAlternatingCechAugmentation_comp_cechAugmentationZero (X.over U)
        (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)))).symm

/-- **The identification `Č(f)|_U ≅ Č(f|_U)` carries the restriction of the augmentation
`Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]` to the augmentation `Č(f|_U) ⟶ 𝒪_U[0]` of the slice.** Both sides are maps into a
complex concentrated in degree zero, so the identity is checked there, where it is
`overFunctor_map_cechAugmentationZero_comp`. -/
theorem overFunctor_map_cechAugmentation_comp :
    ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map (cechAugmentation X f) ≫
        (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).hom =
      (extendedAlternatingCechOverIso X U f).hom ≫
        cechAugmentation (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.to_single_hom_ext ?_
  simp only [HomologicalComplex.comp_f, Functor.mapHomologicalComplex_map_f,
    cechAugmentation_f_zero, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]
  rw [overFunctor_map_singleObjXSelf_inv_comp_restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U,
    overFunctor_map_cechAugmentationZero_comp X U f]
  exact Category.assoc _ _ _

/-- The chain-level compatibility of the augmentations, read in the other direction. -/
theorem extendedAlternatingCechOverIso_inv_comp :
    (extendedAlternatingCechOverIso X U f).inv ≫
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map (cechAugmentation X f) =
      cechAugmentation (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)) ≫
        (restrictStructureSheafComplexOverIso X U).inv :=
  inv_comp_eq_comp_inv_of _ _ (overFunctor_map_cechAugmentation_comp X U f)

/-- **The identification `Č(f)|_U ≅ Č(f|_U)` in the derived category carries the restriction of
the augmentation to the augmentation of the slice**, under the identification
`𝒪[0]|_U ≅ 𝒪_U[0]`. The chain-level statement
`overFunctor_map_cechAugmentation_comp` pushed through the localization functor, the two
identifications of classes of restricted complexes cancelling by the naturality of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restrictionComparison`. -/
theorem overFunctor_mapDerivedCategory_map_cechAugmentation_comp :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f)) ≫
        (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).hom =
      (extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso X U f).hom ≫
        DerivedCategory.Q.map
          (cechAugmentation (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))) := by
  rw [derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso, Iso.trans_hom, ← Category.assoc,
    restrictionComparison_naturality, Category.assoc, Functor.mapIso_hom,
    ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, overFunctor_map_cechAugmentation_comp X U f,
    CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, ← Category.assoc]
  rfl

/-- The same identity with both isomorphisms inverted, which is the form the completion map
consumes. -/
theorem extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso_inv_comp :
    (extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso X U f).inv ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f)) =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map
          (cechAugmentation (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))) ≫
        (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).inv :=
  inv_comp_eq_comp_inv_of _ _ (overFunctor_mapDerivedCategory_map_cechAugmentation_comp X U f)

/-- **The Čech completion map restricts to the Čech completion map of the slice.** Under the
natural isomorphism `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctorRestrictIso`, which identifies
`K^∧|_U` with `(K|_U)^∧`, the restriction of the completion map `K ⟶ K^∧` of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] is the completion map `K|_U ⟶ (K|_U)^∧` of the slice.

The completion map is the identification `K = R𝑆heafHom(𝒪, K)` followed by the map induced by the
augmentation `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]`, so this is the conjunction of two compatibilities: that the
restriction of the augmentation is the augmentation of the slice,
`extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso_inv_comp`, and that the restriction of
`R𝑆heafHom(𝒪, K) ≅ K` is the one of the slice, `derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict`. -/
theorem overFunctor_map_completionUnit_comp
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((completionUnit X f).app K) ≫
        (completionFunctorRestrictIso X U f).hom.app K =
      (completionUnit (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))).app
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) := by
  have hii : ((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso
            (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (structureSheafComplex X)) K).hom ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).inv.op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) =
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).hom ≫
        (@Iso.inv _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K))) :=
    comp_eq_comp_inv_of_comp_comp _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso_restrict X U K)
  have haug : ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
              (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f))).op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso X U f).inv.op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) =
      ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (derivedStructureSheafRestrictIso X U).inv.op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation (X.over U)
              (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)))).op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) := by
    rw [← NatTrans.comp_app, ← NatTrans.comp_app, ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp,
      ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, ← op_comp, ← op_comp,
      extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso_inv_comp X U f]
  show (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((derivedStructureSheafHomIso X K).inv ≫
            ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map
              (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f)).op).app K) ≫
        (((derivedHomRestriction X U).iso
              (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (extendedAlternatingCech X f)) K).hom ≫
          ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
              (extendedAlternatingCechDerivedRestrictIso X U f).inv.op).app
            ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K)) =
      (@Iso.inv _ _ _ _ (derivedStructureSheafHomIso (X.over U) ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K))) ≫
        ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor (X.over U)).map
            (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation (X.over U)
              (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)))).op).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K)
  rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [reassoc_of% ((derivedHomRestriction X U).natural_left
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f))),
    haug, reassoc_of% hii, Iso.map_inv_hom_id_assoc]

/-- **The missing compatibility of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F]**: the completion map of the slice,
followed by the identification `(K|_U)^∧ ≅ K^∧|_U`, is the restriction of the completion map. This
is `overFunctor_map_completionUnit_comp` with the isomorphism inverted. -/
theorem completionUnit_comp_completionFunctorRestrictIso_inv
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    (completionUnit (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) ≫
        (completionFunctorRestrictIso X U f).inv.app K =
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.map
        ((completionUnit X f).app K) := by
  rw [← overFunctor_map_completionUnit_comp X U f K, Category.assoc,
    ← NatTrans.comp_app, Iso.hom_inv_id, NatTrans.id_app]
  exact Category.comp_id _

/-- **The map `a` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] is invertible at an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`:** the
canonical map
`a : (K|_U)^∧ ⟶ K^∧|_U` is an isomorphism, for `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)` generated by a finite family
of global sections and `ℐ|_U = (f_1|_U, …, f_r|_U)` generated on the slice by their restrictions
— which is the restriction of `ℐ`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal_idealOfGlobalSections`.

The reflector of [Stacks, Tag 099F] at each of the two ideal sheaves is the Čech completion
functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B], unit and all, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_derivedCompletion_completionFunctor`; that functor
commutes with restriction to the slice by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctorRestrictIso`, compatibly with the completion maps
by `completionUnit_comp_completionFunctorRestrictIso_inv`. So the composite of those three
isomorphisms is an isomorphism `(K|_U)^∧ ≅ K^∧|_U` carrying one unit to the other, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionRestrictComparison_of_unit_comp` identifies
it with `a`. -/
theorem isIso_derivedCompletionRestrictComparisonGlobalSections_app
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) :
    letI := isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections X f
    letI := isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections (X.over U)
      (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))
    IsIso ((derivedCompletionRestrictComparisonGlobalSections X U f).app K) := by
  letI := isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections X f
  letI := isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections (X.over U)
    (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))
  obtain ⟨θX, hθX⟩ := exists_iso_derivedCompletion_completionFunctor X f K
  obtain ⟨θU, hθU⟩ := exists_iso_derivedCompletion_completionFunctor (X.over U)
    (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i))
    ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj K)
  have hX : (derivedCompletionUnit X (idealOfGlobalSections X f)).app K =
      (completionUnit X f).app K ≫ θX.inv := by
    rw [← hθX, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]
  refine isIso_derivedCompletionRestrictComparison_of_unit_comp X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) U
    (idealOfGlobalSections (X.over U) (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver X U (f i)))
    (mem_idealOfGlobalSections_of_mem_idealOfGlobalSections_over X U f)
    (θU ≪≫ ((completionFunctorRestrictIso X U f).app K).symm ≪≫
